  "comment": "Roll-up choreography (concept delete-concept-v6, neutral gape mouth). Beats: 0.00-0.35 the file fades in at the hand side (window layer) and the pet's eyes find it; 0.35-1.05 the right arm rises and grips while the window layer rolls the file into a paper roll; 1.05-1.45 the body lunges forward (ShiftX 80) and the neutral gape opens wide -- the only fast moment besides the bite; 1.45-1.55 the jaw snaps shut onto the roll (gape drops to 0, window layer shortens the roll and drops crumbs); 1.55-2.55 four chews read as cheek pulses (0.45<->0.75) with a satisfied eye smile, the hand stays up holding the shortening roll; 2.55-3.20 everything settles back to standing. Bite frames write Gape+MouthOpenY, never SmileOpen -- the smile stays an emotion. Gape is DISCRETE (0/1, quantised again in CubismCanvas at the write site): a partial value crossfades the gape switch over the resting omega and renders two mouths in one frame; the opening size is MouthOpenY deforming the opaque gape art. Window-layer sync contract: icon 0.00, roll 0.35-1.05, roll reaches mouth 1.45, roll shortens x4 during chews, crumbs 1.45-2.8.",
